@ukman9234Ehm.. aren't capitalism and communism about economy, and on the other hand autocracy and democracy about distribution of (political) power?

So I acknowledge capitalism and communism to be mutually exclusive, as well as that autocracy (aka dictatorship) and democracy are mutual exclusive, but I don't know that to be the case of communism and autocracy, even though you 'talk' as if such is the case. Could you please explain why (I should think that) this is?

P.S. even though capitalism and communism are mutual exclusive, to consider these as the only two options of describing an economy is a false dichotomy. And the same goes with autocracy and democracy with respect to politic power structures: also a false dichotomy.

