@anjamilde I have not stated that price is the only decision maker when buying a car but for many it is a major factor alongside quality. Germans have been clever to produce cars with "quality impression" which has not that much to do with technical quality (longevity and reliability). 

Japanese cars surpassed German quality already in the late 90's. Chinese are now doing the same surpassing German quality which has not being great for the past decades. So that's correct market advantage has gone. Why would you buy a German premium when you get a Chinese premium for less money ?

German cars being expensive is partly true regarding premiums like MB, BMW, Porche and Audi but not like WV in all of it's reincarnations and Opel.

