​@bsastarfire250 oh, I wasn't trying to say they were cheap. A neighbor bought some for his house and had them professionally installed and I think he said that it took 5 years for them to offset that initial cost. But these days the power company pays him more often than he pays them.

What I was talking about though was the upkeep cost. If you bought a generator that could output the same amout of energy as those solar panels, then you'd need to refuel it pretty regularly. So even if it's cheaper to buy and set up, the constant fuel cost is going to make it more expensive in the long term.

Of course, I might've completely misunderstood the tone of your comment, and it could be that you're agreeing with me. In which case, whoops ^¥^;

