snippet.textDisplay:
@kshred3043 Not all areas were controlled in the same way. It was strange. Some community areas had metal fences erected around them, yet across the road, people could walk around normally. Our building had wire wrapped around the external door handles to stop people going in and out of for several days. While not 'welded' shut, the entire building was shut.

In my opinion, locking everyone down for a month globally could have ended the whole thing quickly, but while some people were allowed out (excluding essential workers), it was always going to go on for a long time.

When people talk about "in China", it is often that little bit they have been in, not the whole country.

