@longrolstral Interesting.  You obviously lived through it.  My information comes second hand from people I know and trust who also lived through it.  One said that it depended on the attitudes of the people in charge of the communities.  Some apparently  let the powers that they had been granted go to their heads and were over zealous.  But, also, they would be judged by not screwing up so would be ultra strict to avoid cases in "their" community.  Another was allowed to wander through the gate of their compound to pick up mail.

"locking everyone down for a month globally could have ended the whole thing quickly,"
Actually, it took 6 weeks of strict lockdown keeping everyone except essential workers in their "bubbles" to totally eliminate the original strain of the virus in New Zealand.  The reward was 16 months (ie: from April 2020 through August 2021 and even longer in the South Island) of essentially covid free while carnage and on-again, off-again lockdowns were the norm in the rest of the world.  That's what competent leadership and social cohesion can achieve.  But it would only take Donald Trump and Fox News to sabotage a global elimination effort.

