snippet.textDisplay:
@Naejje *Will be.* Their fertility rate is somewhere around 1, i.e. there's only 1 child per couple. And it's probably lower, with younger couples often putting off having kids entirely, if they even get together in the first place.

Whether they actually ever had >1B is questionable as well. A Japanese study suggests they were never able to actually feed that many people, with the upper limit being closer to 800M.

How accurate any numbers are is questionable at best, but it's unlikely China is in the habit of underreporting unless a low number would be more benficial. Just the nature of the political system, where not meeting goals is worse than not reporting accurately.

