snippet.textDisplay:
@comicipedia It is not true. it is called AN mode short for autonomous mode. You push the button, you mark it on the map the final destination for truck/car and AI computer inside the car self-drives to what is marked on the map. Chinese cars have this for free but Tesla used to have 1 time payment of 8000$ for AN mode but now, after February 2026, All AN mode licences require a 99$ per month licence. 

Right now, biggest bottle neck is that trucks that are self-driving require something called Safety driver, also sometime refer to as Co-Pilot. In other words, you have a human in vehicle and their entire job is to sit in the truck and refuel the truck with diesel/gas for 18 wheeler. You have to pay these co-pilots the same as you pay a truck driver even though they are not driving. The goal is to remove co-pilot safety drivers and replace them with Optimus robots. Optimus robot just sits in 18 wheeler and their job is to refuel the 18 wheeler truck similar to safety driver. Walmart for example already uses these truck drivers in Texas.

Here is a video on CNN: https://www.cnn.com/2026/08/08/world/video/ai-driverless-truck-ed-lavandera-080802aseg2-cnni-business-fast

