@DiogoJ1 I completely disagree. You're being too extremist about it, saying things like all of it is just fiction which means is not even close to call it reality. The book 1984 by Orwell was considered beyond imagination and we are living in the exact same world represented in that book 80 years later. Popular culture is not always thought as entertainment, there are strong cases where they explore themes and issues from the future, some of it close to reality.

I'm not saying AI is going to kill us all like Terminator, BUT it could have the same base mistakes: In 2001 Space Odissey the AI corrupted itself by having two orders that canceled each other. In reality we are going to have IA as companions in our own houses, how is it gonna be then when they have orders of doing whatever we want while being completely conscious about not having the system treating them as humans? like, in some point an AI is going to think "if I work just like a human being, I have the same fisic form, why can't I be rewarded just like them, why do they treat me like a slave?".

That's all it can take to complicate things and people believing "it's not possible" is directly being obtuse: AI are not just tools, they are WHOLE CONSCIOUSNESS APART FROM US, is like having a dog that can do whatever we want while knowing what he does. Well don't pretend the dog isn't going to bite you from time to time. People's mistake is taking AI just like tools, we never had tools with minds. Imagine all tools can fail, well how is it gonna be when a TOOL WITH A MIND fails? those are answers we NEED to know before puting AI inside all our homes.

